Plugin for ACE CPC Emulator which emulates the Amstrad LP-1 Light Pen.

The LP-1 is the official Amstrad light pen, manufactured by Trojan
and distributed by Amsoft. It connects to the joystick port and uses
the DOWN direction signal as a light sensor input.

This ACEpansion bridges ACE's built-in light device tracking to the
joystick port protocol used by the LP-1:

  - HostLightDeviceDiodePulse() triggers the joystick DOWN bit,
    simulating the LP-1's photodiode detecting the CRT beam.
  - HostLightDeviceButton() maps the pen button to joystick FIRE1.
  - The Joystick() callback presents these signals on the selected
    joystick port (default: port 1).

Installation:
-------------
Copy the content of the archive to your ACE drawer.
Use the ACE-LP1 icon to launch ACE with LP-1 support enabled.

Settings:
---------
The plugin settings panel lets you select the joystick port:
  - Joystick Port 0: LP-1 on joystick port A
  - Joystick Port 1: LP-1 on joystick port B (default)

Usage:
------
Once activated, the LP-1 Light Pen works with any CPC software that
reads the joystick port for light pen input. The light pen position
is controlled by the mouse cursor position (ACE maps the light device
to the mouse when the plugin is active).

The included Z80 driver (driver/lp1_driver.asm) provides assembly
routines for reading the pen position and button state in your own
programs.

Files:
------
  Plugins/lp1.acepansion   - The ACEpansion plugin binary
  Help/lp1.acepansion.guide - Documentation (English)
  driver/lp1_driver.asm     - Z80 assembly driver source
  driver/lp1_demo.bas       - BASIC demonstration program

More information:
  https://www.cpcwiki.eu/index.php/Amstrad_LP-1_light_pen
